      "body": "## Summary\n\n- Treat `val_size == 1` as an absolute sample count, consistently with larger integer counts and the documented `[0, 1)` fractional range.\n- Add eight regression cases covering CLI `1`/`1.0`, larger counts, fractional splits, and streaming/non-streaming integer and float inputs.\n\n`DataArguments.val_size` is typed as `float`, so `HfArgumentParser` converts `--val_size 1` to `1.0`. The existing `> 1` conversion leaves that boundary as a float, which `Dataset.train_test_split()` rejects. Changing the boundary to `>= 1` reserves one validation sample instead. This also preserves the existing streaming behavior. The older fix referenced by #474 handled values greater than one; this fixes the remaining equality boundary rather than reopening that report.\n\n## Validation\n\nFresh validation against base `47d407d2aabbd52e11d4f34c7a06b9de3e2f0a77` and this exact patch, using Python 3.12.14, PyTorch 2.5.1+cpu, Transformers 4.57.1, Datasets 4.0.0, pytest 8.4.2, and Ruff 0.15.5:\n\n```sh\nWANDB_DISABLED=true pytest -vv --import-mode=importlib tests/data/test_data_utils.py tests/data/test_converter.py\nWANDB_DISABLED=true pytest -vv --import-mode=importlib tests/data/test_formatter.py\nruff check src/llamafactory/data/data_utils.py tests/data/test_data_utils.py\nruff format --check src/llamafactory/data/data_utils.py tests/data/test_data_utils.py\npython tests/check_license.py scripts src tests tests_v1\n```\n\n- Regression plus existing converter tests: **10 passed** on the fix; the same tests on the base produced **3 failed, 7 passed**, with failures specifically for CLI `1`, CLI `1.0`, and non-streaming `val_size=1.0` (`ValueError: test_size=1.0`).\n- Existing formatter tests: **50 passed** on the fix.\n- Changed-file lint/format and repository license-header checks: passed.\n- Repository-wide Ruff checks are not green: base and patch produce identical pre-existing `W293` at `src/llamafactory/model/patcher.py:486` and formatting findings in `data/template.py`, `data/tool_utils.py`, `model/patcher.py`, and `v1/plugins/model_plugins/kernels/ops/rms_norm/supa_rms_norm.py`.\n- Full-suite collection is blocked by the installed PyTorch 2.5.1+cpu version by `tests_v1/conftest.py` requiring `torch.accelerator` (PyTorch >=2.7). The full suite was **not run**; model/tokenizer-dependent tests and training were not executed. Tests above used offline Hugging Face settings, disabled telemetry, and an external-network guard; no model assets were downloaded.\n\nThis is an AI-assisted contribution; the change and regression behavior were reviewed and tested. No claim of a full-suite or upstream CI pass is intended.\n\nFinal combined candidate run: **60 passed**, 2026-10-31 04:45:30 UTC. Base full collection confirmed the identical v1 torch.accelerator prerequisite failure.\n\n## Before submitting\n\n- [x] Read the contributor guideline.\n- [x] Added the necessary regression tests.\n",
